# Template Rules — GoCaSE

## Base Layout
- ALL page templates must wrap content in the shared layout:
  ```html
  {{template "layout" .}}
  ```
- The layout is defined in `views/layout.html` and provides: navbar, footer, CSS variables, TailwindCSS CDN, HTMX CDN

## Template Data
- Template data is `map[string]interface{}` — access with `.KeyName`
- The session object is always available as `.Session` (may be nil on public pages — always guard with `{{if .Session}}`)
- `.Session.UserID`, `.Session.Username`, `.Session.Role`, `.Session.AppVersion` are the available session fields

## CSS / Styling
- Use Tailwind utility classes — do not write custom CSS inline
- Use the semantic design tokens defined in layout.html: `--edu-primary`, `--edu-accent`, `--edu-bg`, `--edu-surface`
- Reusable component classes: `app-card`, `app-input`, `btn`, `btn-primary`, `btn-secondary`, `btn-accent`
- Page headings use `page-title` class; subtitles use `page-subtitle` class

## HTMX
- Use `hx-post`, `hx-get`, `hx-target`, `hx-swap` for dynamic interactions
- Always set `hx-headers='{"X-Requested-With": "XMLHttpRequest"}'` on HTMX requests that need JSON error responses
- Partial responses (HTMX targets) do NOT use the layout wrapper

## Security
- Never output raw HTML with `{{.Value | html}}` unless the source is trusted admin content
- User-supplied content must use `{{.Value}}` (auto-escaped by html/template)
- CSRF: all state-changing forms must POST to a handler that validates session ownership

## Accessibility
- Every `<input>` must have a corresponding `<label for="...">` or `aria-label`
- Buttons must have visible text or `aria-label`
- Use semantic HTML: `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<footer>`, `<section>`, `<article>` appropriately
